---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ArticleHero from '../components/ArticleHero.astro';
const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'AboutPage',
  name: 'About Sola Hair Salon',
};
---
<Layout
  title="About | Sola Hair Salon"
  description="Learn about Sola Hair Salon, our editorial approach, and our independence from Sola Salon Studios."
  canonicalPath="/about/"
  schema={schema}
>
  <ArticleHero eyebrow="About" title="About Sola Hair Salon" image="/images/gallery/gallery-education-event.jpg" imageAlt="Salon education and training event" />
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-14">
    <p class="text-ink/80 leading-relaxed mb-6">
      Sola Hair Salon is an independent, editorially run resource covering the
      salon-studio model, hair services, hairstyles, hair care and salon pricing. Our
      goal is to give people clear, practical information before they book an
      appointment — nothing more.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3">Why This Site Exists</h2>
    <p class="text-ink/80 leading-relaxed mb-6">
      Searching for information about salon studios, salon pricing, or which
      haircut suits a particular face shape tends to turn up either official
      marketing pages or scattered, inconsistent forum advice. We started this
      site to sit in between those two extremes: independent enough to be candid
      about trade-offs and pricing realities, but organized and thorough enough to
      actually answer the question you came with. Every guide is written to
      answer one specific question completely, rather than padding out a topic
      with filler to rank for a keyword.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3">Independence</h2>
    <p class="text-ink/80 leading-relaxed mb-6">
      We are not affiliated with, sponsored by, or endorsed by Sola Salon Studios.
      We reference the brand only to describe and inform, and we do not use Sola's
      logos, trademarks, or official branding. Nothing on this site should be read
      as an official statement from, or authorized directory of, Sola Salon
      Studios or any specific location or professional working within that model.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3">How We Approach the Free Tools</h2>
    <p class="text-ink/80 leading-relaxed mb-6">
      Our Salon Cost Calculator and Hair Length Calculator are built to be
      genuinely useful starting points, not lead-generation gimmicks. Both run
      entirely in your browser — no account, no email capture, no data sent to a
      server — and both are clearly labeled as estimates rather than exact quotes,
      because that's what they actually are. We'd rather a tool underpromise and
      be transparent about its limits than present a rough calculation as
      something more precise than it is.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3">Editorial Principles</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-ink/80 mb-6">
      <li>Every article is written or reviewed by a human before publishing.</li>
      <li>We don't publish scraped, spun, or copied content.</li>
      <li>We don't fabricate statistics, reviews, or professional credentials.</li>
      <li>Factual claims are checked against reliable sources where relevant.</li>
      <li>We don't run ads that interrupt reading, and we don't design pages primarily around advertising.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3">What We're Still Building</h2>
    <p class="text-ink/80 leading-relaxed mb-6">
      This site is actively growing — new guides are added regularly, following
      the same questions people most often bring into a salon consultation.
      If you've read something here that felt incomplete, outdated, or just
      plain wrong, we genuinely want to hear about it and fix it, rather than let
      it sit.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3">What Makes a Guide "Original" Here</h2>
    <p class="text-ink/80 leading-relaxed mb-6">
      We take "original content" seriously in a specific, practical sense: every
      guide is written from scratch for this site, drawing on general, widely
      understood knowledge about hair services and salon business practices
      rather than being rewritten from any single competing source. Where a claim
      needs a factual anchor beyond general knowledge, we aim to check it rather
      than assume it's correct because it's commonly repeated elsewhere online.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3">A Note on Advertising</h2>
    <p class="text-ink/80 leading-relaxed mb-6">
      This site may eventually carry advertising to help sustain the work of
      researching and writing new guides, but ads are never allowed to determine
      what we recommend or how we describe a service, technique, or pricing
      range. If a page ever carries a sponsored placement, it will be clearly
      labeled as such — nothing here is designed to look like independent advice
      while secretly being paid promotion.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3">Who's Behind This Site</h2>
    <p class="text-ink/80 leading-relaxed mb-6">
      Sola Hair Salon is run as a small, focused editorial project rather than a
      large publication with a masthead of contributors. Content is researched,
      written, and reviewed with an emphasis on accuracy and practical
      usefulness over volume — we would rather publish twenty genuinely
      thorough guides than two hundred thin ones. As the site grows, any named
      contributors will be introduced here with their actual background, and we
      won't claim credentials that aren't real.
    </p>

    <p class="text-ink/80 leading-relaxed">
      Questions or corrections? Visit our <a href="/contact/" class="text-rose-600 underline">Contact page</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
